[Music]  [Music]  the world chess hall of fame  has been open in st louis for nine years  now but it did exist prior to its  opening  in september of 2011.  it moved here from miami florida and was  in washington dc  and in new york before that after the  museum in miami closed in 2008 it just  happened to be the exact same time that  the st  louis chess club opened in st louis in  the central west  end it made such a perfect fit to move  that museum here to st louis our mission  at the world chess hall of fame is to  educate visitors about  the rich cultural and educational  history  of the game of chess according to the  world chess federation  over 600 million people play chess  they're from all over the world they're  from all different groups and cultures  so whether you're a chess player or  you've never  played the game before you can come in  here  and really be inspired by by our  programming  in 2019 we had over 23 000 visitors  and that was the largest group of people  that we had entered into the building in  one year so we're really happy about  that  obviously because of covid19 we did have  to close temporarily  but we are open we're taking great  precautions to keep our staff  and our visitors safe and healthy and we  are starting to see our numbers go back  up and we've been really adapting  with kind of new ways of reaching our  audiences  through our programming and our music  series we're all wearing masks  we have hand sanitizer stations we do  health questionnaires and temperature  screenings before visitors come  in we also have a rich array of  educational programming available  throughout our website and on our  youtube page so if you can't come in and  see our exhibitions you can still learn  about them  on our website i would like to thank all  of our supporters  especially dr jeannie karen singfield  and rex singfield  for all they do for chess in st louis  and around the world  you

